/*****************************************************************************
    IBkant -- the kant wiki as a kant form: kant describing itself (Tony, 2026-11-13).
    THE SKELETON. Definitions only, shaped like firstLight; to fire it see Topics/forms, Firing a form by hand.
    The includer loads utilities and styles and searches cOLOr, fONTs and sTYLEs first.
    Three pages, each a form of its own. The window holds one of them in its page field
    (form:=ibPage); a click on an entry of the contents writes ibPage, and ibPage's
    listener redraws. The words are poured by name from IncantForms/IBkant/text.
*****************************************************************************/
registry(fILEs);
define
    ibkantTextFile File='IncantForms/IBkant/text';
    ;
include(ibkantTextFile);
register(FORMs);
define
    ibWelcome window x=0 y=0 width=440 height=440 down fill:=white font:=normalFont color:=blue
        ibWelcomeHead="I be kant" text height=44 font:=titleFont color:=green bottomBorder;
        ibWelcomeBody="{IBkantText.welcomeOne}\n\n{IBkantText.welcomeTwo}" text align=justify;
    ;
define
    ibFields window x=0 y=0 width=440 height=440 down fill:=white font:=normalFont color:=blue
        ibFieldsHead="Fields" text height=44 font:=titleFont color:=green bottomBorder;
        ibFieldsBody="{IBkantText.fieldsOne}\n\n{IBkantText.fieldsTwo}" text align=justify;
    ;
define
    ibForms window x=0 y=0 width=440 height=440 down fill:=white font:=normalFont color:=blue
        ibFormsHead="Forms" text height=44 font:=titleFont color:=green bottomBorder;
        ibFormsBody="{IBkantText.formsOne}\n\n{IBkantText.formsTwo}" text align=justify;
    ;
define
    ibPage;
    ;
ibPage := ibWelcome;
define
    showWelcome code={ ibPage := ibWelcome; };
    showFields code={ ibPage := ibFields; };
    showForms code={ ibPage := ibForms; };
    ;
define
    IBkant window x=200 y=200 width=600 height=500 down fill:=wall font:=normalFont color:=blue
        ibTitle="IBkant" text height=60 font:=titleFont color:=green align=center valign=center bottomBorder;
        ibMain across
            ibContents width=160 down
                toWelcome="Welcome" text height=34 border fill:=lightGreen align=center valign=center onClick:=showWelcome;
                toFields="Fields" text height=34 border fill:=lightGreen align=center valign=center onClick:=showFields;
                toForms="Forms" text height=34 border fill:=lightGreen align=center valign=center onClick:=showForms;
                ibRest;
            ibPageField form:=ibPage;
    ;
bail();

HOW IT WORKS. Every piece is one built today (Topics/forms G2; Topics/typesetting T3):
    a form inside a field     ibPageField form:=ibPage. ibPage is a field of its own that holds the page form.
    the swap                  writing ibPage (ibPage := ibFields) tells its listener, which calls redrawForm.
    the click                 click(request) on toFields fires its onClick, showFields, which writes ibPage.
    words by name             a page body is {IBkantText.fieldsOne}: the passage is poured from the text file.
To add a page: its passages in IncantForms/IBkant/text; a page form, a show action and a contents entry here.
Not here yet: a real click (windows, forms step 10); which entry is selected is not shown; a passage is one paragraph.

TO FIRE IT: the lines are in Topics/forms, under "Firing a form by hand" (and dormant in IncantForms/WorkingOn/tester, below its stop()).
